{"id":"79eb78b7242498b56086ea0cb692dd9f44a8e70067e8f7a962a15bb4bea890c0","lamport":0,"author":"scual.project@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-09-27T11:01:42.586650024Z","format_version":1,"kind":"create","payload":{"fields":{"created-at":"2026-09-27T11:01:42.586650024Z","created-by":"scual.project@gmail.com","description":"Many commands default to the checked-out ticket when no id is given, but flags that take a required ticket value (e.g. `ti list --blocks X`, `--depends-on X` from 2870b8) cannot default because `ti list` has a positional view-name argument, making an optional flag value ambiguous.\n\nProposal: a sentinel such as `.` or `@` accepted anywhere a ticket reference is accepted, resolving to the checked-out ticket (e.g. `ti list --blocks .`).\n\nOpen questions:\n- Which sentinel (`.`, `@`, `HEAD`-like word) and whether it can collide with id prefixes or view names.\n- Resolve at the id-resolution layer so every command gets it for free.\n- Saved views: store the resolved full id, not the sentinel (consistent with 2870b8).\n\nRelated: 2870b8.","state":"new","status":"open","title":"CLI-wide sentinel for \"the checked-out ticket\""}}}